# Symbol libraries Vellum loads at start-up, one file per line.  ALL of
# them stay loaded (so any drawing's symbols resolve); the palette shows
# one at a time -- its header cell switches between them, and the toolbar
# Lib button loads further files.  The user scratch library SymEdit edits by
# default (/usr/vellum/etc/symbols) is always tried after these.
/usr/vellum/sym/discrete.sym
/usr/vellum/sym/logic.sym
/usr/vellum/sym/flow.sym
/usr/vellum/sym/net.sym
/usr/vellum/sym/arch.sym
/usr/vellum/sym/pid.sym
/usr/vellum/sym/power.sym
/usr/vellum/sym/plan.sym
